{"duration_api_ms":104034,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"8e77ff04-6982-41dc-913c-897dbd3ccc89","total_cost_usd":0.829174,"usage":{"input_tokens":24562,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":371328,"output_tokens":20828,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"bench-model":{"inputTokens":24562,"outputTokens":20828,"cacheReadInputTokens":371328,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.829174,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"bench-model","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"unknown"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":20,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"Implemented both pieces:\n\n**`src/sun.js` — `sunPosition`** (`src/sun.js:59`)\n- Standard SunCalc chain: Julian days → solar mean anomaly → equation of the centre/ecliptic longitude → declination and right ascension → hour angle.\n- Returns `alt` (radians above horizon) and `bearing` converted from SunCalc's south-to-west azimuth to a compass bearing clockwise from north, wrapped to `[0, 2π)`.\n\n**`src/shade.js` — `shadeAt`** (`src/shade.js:68`)\n- Returns `null` when `alt <= 0`.\n- Samples each court's `pl × pw` playing area at 1 m grid centres, transformed through `fromFrame`.\n- For every sample, walks the obstacle grid toward the sun with an Amanatides–Woo DDA (matching `cellOf`'s row/column layout), comparing each cell's top (`top[c] / 10`, ignoring `-32768`) against the ray height `z + distance · tan(alt)`.\n- Uses the ray's entry distance into each cell (the lowest point of the ray over that cell), so a cell blocks only when its top actually rises above the ray. Marching stops at the venue edge, so obstacles beyond the grid never count.\n\nVerification:\n- `node --test`: 4/4 pass.\n- Sanity checks confirmed sun positions (Seattle June midday alt ≈ 66°, south; night below horizon) and directional shading: an east wall shades in the morning only, a west wall in the evening, a south wall at noon, short walls don't block high sun, and raising the court elevation stops a wall from blocking. A brute-force ray-stepping comparison agreed with the DDA within sampling tolerance.","ttft_ms":1521,"type":"result","duration_ms":105320,"uuid":"0e979e92-94e4-4fc4-99a8-53c10e7268ed","ttft_stream_ms":602,"time_to_request_ms":47,"first_content_frame_ms":602,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
